fix: simplify tournament admin setup per live usage feedback

After running the new admin dashboard live, several fields turned out
to be unnecessary busywork rather than useful configuration:

- Registration open/close is a manual admin action (Open Registration
  / Lock Registration buttons), not something worth pre-scheduling —
  drops registrationOpensAt/registrationClosesAt and the "closes in"
  countdown on the public page.
- Eligible-slots curation added admin overhead for no real fairness
  benefit — entrants can now name any slot at registration (web form
  uses the full slot-catalog picker; chat entry accepts any slot text),
  the same permissive pattern Bonus Bingo already uses. Drops
  Tournament.eligibleSlots and the TournamentScoringMethod enum's
  sibling fields (scoringMethod, spinsPerMatch) which were purely
  descriptive and never drove any logic anyway.
- Drops the per-tournament Audit Log tab and its backend endpoint
  entirely — not needed for this feature.

Also fixes the admin tournament list stacking every past tournament
above the active one's control panel as more get created — completed/
cancelled tournaments now collapse into a "History (N)" toggle instead
of piling up at the top.

